  "body": "# Associated User Story\nAs a user, I want to be able to submit an event that is not a PT event to an officer for approval, but can count towards my points.\n\nAs an officer, I want a window where I can see forms for members submitting proposals for outside special events to count towards their point total.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n### Members can submit a non-PT event for officer review, and once an officer approves it, the points are added to the member's total and the correct point type.\n- Sunny: A member fills out a submission form with the event name, date, point type (e.g., service, personal development, social), and a short description or proof of attendance, then submits it. The member sees a confirmation and the request shows as \"pending\" in their dashboard. Officers see the request in an approval queue with all the submitted details. When an officer approves it, the points are added to the member's dashboard under the correct point type, their active status updates if they now meet the minimums, and the member sees the status change to \"approved.\" Pending and denied requests never add points. If an officer denies it, the member sees \"denied\" along with the officer's reason.\n- Rainy: A member submits with a required field missing, an invalid date, or a duplicate of an event they already submitted, the submission fails to send, or a regular member tries to approve or deny a request. The system shows a clear error message (e.g., \"Please fill in all required fields\" or \"Your submission could not be sent, try again or contact an officer\") instead of failing silently or losing what the member entered. No points are added until an officer approves, and if an approval fails to save, the request stays pending and the points are not counted so totals are never wrong. Only officers can access the approval queue and approve or deny requests.\n### Officers have a dedicated window that lists all member-submitted proposals for outside special events, with the full form details and the ability to approve or deny each one.\n- Sunny: An officer opens the proposals window and sees a list of submitted forms showing the member's name, event name, date, point type, description or proof, and status (pending, approved, or denied). They can filter by status, open any form to see its full details, and approve or deny it with an optional reason. When a proposal is approved, the points are added to that member's total and correct point type, and the member sees the updated status. Pending and denied proposals never add points.\n- Rainy: The proposals fail to load, there are no submissions yet, an approval or denial fails to save, or a regular member tries to open the window. The system shows a clear message (e.g., \"Proposals could not be loaded, try again later\" or \"No proposals to review\") instead of a blank page or wrong information. If a decision fails to save, the proposal stays pending and no points are added so totals are never wrong, and only officers can access the window.\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
